From 4603041d34f5f3c66bc9b40fa71989e1144b40ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:11:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 45/59] docs, gui: encryption wording for the release notes

- Compatibility with proxmox-backup-client is stated as verified in CI (e2e
  tests 3 and 9: official key, official restore, refused without the key; our
  read-back of an official encrypted disk backup).
- "signed manifest" dropped from the public text: AES-256-GCM and the
  compatibility say what users need.
- Importing a passphrase-protected key in the GUI saves the new key file
  without a passphrase: said in the CHANGELOG and READMEs, and shown as a
  warning in the import panel (5 languages).
---
 CHANGELOG.md                                   | 18 ++++++++++++------
 README.fr.md                                   | 12 +++++++++---
 README.md                                      | 13 +++++++++----
 .../src/components/EncryptionKeyField.jsx      |  3 +++
 gui/frontend/src/i18n/translations.js          |  5 +++++
 5 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

